/- Lean-first (no Rocq counterpart).

# The authentication example's closed theorem (stage S2 of the `etcd_auth_safe` Scope, 2026-11-13)

A closed theorem about the operational semantics of `authkv`'s program (`examples/etcd/auth`): the
package's initialization (which initializes its import closure: etcd's server with its auth store,
its gRPC layer, the client, raft, ...) followed by `Main()` -- one etcd member started in process
with the simple token provider, a client with no user that sets up the auth state (root with the
root role, role `r` granted `READWRITE` on `[a, b)`, users `u` with `r` and `v` with no role) and
enables auth, clients authenticated as root, `u` and `v`, the four principals' workloads at once
(`u`, `v`, a client with no token, the same client with a token no provider issued), root's last
write `z/end`, root's watch of every key from revision `1` read up to it with the history's check,
and `u`'s watch of `[a, b)` -- started from a fresh state (no package initialized, one thread): for
every real execution of `n` steps, the main thread's result, if it has one, is `Ok` (`0`),
`Failed` (`1`) or `WatchEnded` (`2`), no thread is stuck, and no thread has ended in a panic (in
particular none of `Main`'s checks panicked: `Spec/.../auth/Main.lean` says what each check
means, and `Results.lean`'s `etcd_auth_safe` what the result does not say).

It is a copy of watchkv's (`watch/Adequacy.lean`), at authkv's program, client address
`127.0.0.1:23916`, data directory `authkv.etcd` and member `authkv`, from `authkv`'s
`wp_initialize'` (`Init.lean`, over `PkgTable.lean`, both generated by `etc/gen-init.py`) and
`etcd_auth.wp_Main` (`Link.lean`) over the member's start with auth on (`startServer.lean`, at
`server_new_auth_on` and `server_Start`, as `Results.lean`'s `authkv_startServer`). Nothing auth-specific is allocated here: `Main` allocates the auth slot itself
(`ak_alloc`, `on γa`).

**Its hypotheses** are watchkv's (`etcd_watch_adequate`, putget's and the watch client's) at
authkv's configuration (`etcd_auth.premises`, putget's with `AuthToken = "simple"`), without
watchkv's bounds on `nw`/`nops` (`Main` takes no argument), and one more: **`hD22`**, D22's
`authSchemaSrv` (`etcdserver/AuthSrv.lean`), the trusted text of the auth store's backend
(`storage/schema`'s auth buckets over the backend) with auth on, a named hypothesis and not an axiom,
so `#print axioms` does not show it (reviewed whole by the axiom skill, refuted four ways and fixed
by stage auth-schema-fix, re-reviewed 2026-11-13: `notes/auth-schema-srv-refuted.md`,
`notes/auth-unknown-fields-nested.md`; discharging it is D22's own track).
-/
module

